## CODE CONVENTIONS

### Language & Framework

- Python 3.11+
- Pydantic v2 for all schema models
- SQLite (stdlib sqlite3) for bi-temporal store
- pytest + pytest-cov for testing

### Schema Patterns

- All bead models inherit from BeadCore (schema/core.py)
- Use `@model_validator(mode='after')` for cross-field validation
  (e.g., OBSERVATION requires WT, PATTERN requires null WT)
- Enums live in schema/enums.py (shared, never duplicated)
- Type-specific content models compose into BeadCore via `content` field

### Integrity Patterns

- Canonical JSON: `json.dumps(obj, sort_keys=True, separators=(',', ':'), ensure_ascii=False)`
- Hash input: ALL fields EXCEPT hash_self and merkle_batch_id
- UUID v7 for bead_id (time-ordered, use uuid6 library)
- HLC for knowledge_time (monotonic, microsecond precision, thread-safe)

### Store Patterns

- Parameterized queries ONLY (no raw string interpolation, no f-strings in SQL)
- Version-tracked migrations (numbered, with rollback support)
- INSERT only for bead content (INV-BEAD-IMMUTABLE)
- UPDATE allowed only on: status, superseded_by, retraction_reason, merkle_batch_id

### Testing Patterns

- Shared fixtures in conftest.py (temp DB, test beads, test keys)
- Invariant tests named `test_inv_*` (e.g., test_inv_bead_immutable)
- Test both happy path AND rejection/error cases for every schema
- Integration tests on actual signing library API (no mock interfaces)
- Target: 200+ tests total across all phases

### Git Discipline

- Commit format: `[Gate1/Area] Brief description`
- Tests MUST pass before every commit
- Zero TODO/FIXME/HACK in committed code
- Update docs/BEAD_FIELD_SPRINT.md running score after milestones
- Report blockers immediately (don't guess at solutions)

